WEBVTT

00:29.195 --> 00:31.698
Ryohei,
don't be late for your interview today.

00:35.952 --> 00:38.079
Are killing games that much fun?

01:21.623 --> 01:25.043
13 MINUTES EARLIER

01:38.932 --> 01:40.683
There's still no game.

01:42.852 --> 01:44.270
Has it been an hour yet?

01:45.104 --> 01:47.982
They must have forgotten
to push the start button.

01:48.983 --> 01:50.944
And what about
the explanation of the rules?

02:05.875 --> 02:06.709
What's wrong?

02:10.755 --> 02:11.756
I can hear something.

02:37.907 --> 02:39.784
Those are cars from the Beach.

03:09.689 --> 03:10.523
It's you guys.

03:11.941 --> 03:13.109
What are you doing here?

03:13.192 --> 03:14.485
We saw the blimps.

03:15.194 --> 03:17.655
And we heard rumors that
the next stage was starting.

03:18.323 --> 03:19.157
Well…

03:20.533 --> 03:21.367
Actually…

03:28.708 --> 03:29.626
A rifle.

03:30.293 --> 03:31.210
Get out of here!

03:31.294 --> 03:32.462
Hide behind the cars!

03:32.545 --> 03:34.589
It's an anti-tank rifle.

03:36.925 --> 03:39.677
Hiding behind a car is pointless.

03:40.178 --> 03:41.012
Holy shit!

03:41.095 --> 03:42.096
Oh, fuck!

03:43.723 --> 03:44.891
Run!

03:49.354 --> 03:50.563
Has the game started?

03:50.647 --> 03:51.522
I don't know.

03:51.606 --> 03:52.815
Did they explain the rules?

03:52.899 --> 03:55.235
There aren't rules! It's just mass murder!

03:58.321 --> 04:00.448
That rifle can fire from a kilometer away.

04:02.617 --> 04:04.869
I've heard the sound of that gun before.

04:05.370 --> 04:07.330
Now they're using an assault rifle.

04:07.413 --> 04:08.998
We don't know how many there are.

04:09.082 --> 04:10.875
Other players are arriving too!

04:11.626 --> 04:12.961
There could be multiple shooters.

04:13.753 --> 04:15.838
Look how many people still survived!

04:15.922 --> 04:17.006
Run!

04:18.424 --> 04:19.634
They're coming this way.

04:20.468 --> 04:21.469
We have to go!

04:21.970 --> 04:22.804
Seriously?

04:28.768 --> 04:29.602
Let's go!

04:31.521 --> 04:32.355
Arisu!

04:33.606 --> 04:34.691
This is fucked up!

04:35.692 --> 04:36.818
Split up and run!

05:26.743 --> 05:28.161
Arisu, over here!

05:57.774 --> 05:58.608
Crap!

06:01.486 --> 06:03.321
- Shit.
- Skipped your interview again?

06:04.781 --> 06:06.616
If only we could reset reality.

06:13.706 --> 06:14.707
Arisu!

06:39.524 --> 06:40.983
You'll die if you don't stay focused!

06:43.653 --> 06:45.154
Where the fuck are they shooting from?

06:52.995 --> 06:54.580
The King of Spades.

08:43.648 --> 08:45.900
Here you go. A good luck charm.

08:47.026 --> 08:49.403
What's this? A bomb?

08:49.946 --> 08:51.364
Use it when you're in a pinch.

08:53.991 --> 08:55.493
Arisu, we can make it now!

08:58.079 --> 08:58.913
Let's go!

09:03.000 --> 09:04.585
- Arisu!
- He's still alive!

09:06.587 --> 09:08.005
Hey! Stay awake!

09:19.141 --> 09:20.726
The King of Spades…

09:24.981 --> 09:26.023
Hurry!

09:26.107 --> 09:27.275
Stay awake!

09:27.984 --> 09:28.818
Stand up!

09:42.039 --> 09:42.957
You okay?

09:49.505 --> 09:51.507
Are you guys hurt?

09:54.468 --> 09:56.220
It's no good! Run!

09:59.849 --> 10:01.225
The King of Spades…

10:02.602 --> 10:03.811
He's alone?

10:07.189 --> 10:08.232
We're screwed here!

10:08.316 --> 10:09.900
We'll get shot if we run!

10:20.286 --> 10:21.370
Get in!

10:21.454 --> 10:22.371
Tatta!

10:22.455 --> 10:24.081
- Hurry up and get in!
- Ann!

10:30.921 --> 10:32.298
Run, would you?

10:34.425 --> 10:35.468
Shit! Drive!

10:35.551 --> 10:36.594
Step on it!

10:37.887 --> 10:39.138
Chishiya!

10:55.738 --> 10:57.239
Yes! We lost them!

10:57.823 --> 10:59.158
You think Chishiya's okay?

10:59.241 --> 11:00.701
He'll be fine on his own.

11:00.785 --> 11:02.203
What's with this game?

11:02.286 --> 11:04.622
What are the rules?
We didn't even register for it!

11:05.122 --> 11:06.749
Maybe we have to defeat the enemies.

11:06.832 --> 11:08.959
- How many?
- Probably just one.

11:10.753 --> 11:12.171
The King of Spades alone.

11:12.880 --> 11:15.216
It's a battle of strength.
He's the toughest last boss.

11:16.008 --> 11:18.761
That blimp was on the move
while he was firing.

11:19.512 --> 11:22.181
The game arena could be this whole city.

11:22.264 --> 11:24.642
How can we fight
when we've got no weapons?

11:24.725 --> 11:27.436
This next stage
is even tougher than the last.

11:28.437 --> 11:29.605
The next stage…

11:31.148 --> 11:34.819
Let's have some fun together!

11:35.319 --> 11:37.655
Who the heck is Mira anyway?
Is she even human?

11:38.406 --> 11:39.240
I don't know.

11:39.740 --> 11:43.077
But one thing is for sure,
she's involved in making these games.

11:43.160 --> 11:45.496
Mira? She's behind the games?

11:46.080 --> 11:47.998
If that guy earlier
was the King of Spades,

11:48.499 --> 11:51.335
then there must be a game master
for each face card.

11:52.086 --> 11:55.214
Once all of them are defeated,
the next stage is cleared.

11:56.006 --> 11:57.466
Once we do that…

11:57.550 --> 11:58.717
What will happen?

11:58.801 --> 12:00.010
We can go back?

12:03.180 --> 12:04.265
I don't know.

12:04.348 --> 12:06.267
But it's the only way to survive.

12:13.524 --> 12:16.068
Hey, where the heck are we going?

12:16.152 --> 12:19.029
What? I'm just following
that car up ahead.

12:19.113 --> 12:21.073
What? Is that even a good idea?

12:21.157 --> 12:22.408
Where are we supposed to go?

12:22.491 --> 12:25.661
Quit arguing!
At least we got away from that game.

12:25.744 --> 12:27.455
That was no damn game!

12:27.538 --> 12:30.666
Hey, maybe we can just keep running.

12:31.167 --> 12:32.334
We'd never win that game.

12:32.418 --> 12:35.421
That's a good idea.
We've still got lots of time on our visas.

12:35.504 --> 12:39.133
Good point.
Someone else can clear the game for us.

12:45.931 --> 12:46.849
What the fuck?

12:55.316 --> 12:58.110
Just because
all the face card games are cleared

12:58.194 --> 13:00.446
doesn't mean we can go back.

13:01.113 --> 13:03.073
You still believe Hatter's bullshit?

13:03.991 --> 13:07.578
But the next stage started
after we got all 40 cards.

13:09.455 --> 13:11.707
One day,
we all just ended up in this world.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.876
When we cleared games,

13:13.959 --> 13:16.504
we got days added to our visa
depending on the card number.

13:16.587 --> 13:17.755
That's how we can stay alive.

13:18.255 --> 13:21.258
When our visa runs out,
we're killed by that laser.

13:22.343 --> 13:25.888
As Hatter said, we can go home
when we get all the cards.

13:27.014 --> 13:28.641
It seems like a natural rule.

13:29.642 --> 13:31.185
You just want to believe that's true.

13:31.894 --> 13:34.480
All the games we've played
have stuck to their rules.

13:35.481 --> 13:38.651
Even though they're absurd,
they followed simple rules.

13:49.453 --> 13:50.621
It's the guys from the Beach.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.584
Tatta, get away from him!

13:55.668 --> 13:56.919
Hold on!

13:57.002 --> 13:57.836
Tatta!

14:17.648 --> 14:19.650
Tatta! Get us out of here!

14:19.733 --> 14:20.734
- How?
- Tatta!

14:25.281 --> 14:26.323
Let me drive.

14:26.407 --> 14:27.950
- What?
- Now!

14:28.033 --> 14:29.785
- Are you insane?
- Out of the way!

14:29.869 --> 14:31.120
Ann, you sure about this?

14:33.372 --> 14:34.456
Hold on tight!

16:05.923 --> 16:06.966
We pulled away!

16:07.049 --> 16:09.134
- Yes!
- Way to go, Ann!

16:12.930 --> 16:13.806
He's back!

16:39.289 --> 16:40.833
Hey, Ann! Why are you driving here?

17:40.100 --> 17:41.060
You all right?

17:41.143 --> 17:42.519
I twisted my neck.

17:43.270 --> 17:44.354
My nails are broken.

17:44.855 --> 17:45.773
He's coming back!

18:13.801 --> 18:16.595
I can't take it anymore. I can't!

18:16.678 --> 18:18.639
You'll get killed here. Let's go.

18:18.722 --> 18:21.809
Even if I fight,
I'll just have to play another game!

18:21.892 --> 18:23.310
I can't take it anymore!

19:04.393 --> 19:07.104
I don't hear gunshots anymore.
He must be pretty far away.

19:09.481 --> 19:11.108
- Let's stay here for a while.
- Yeah.

19:11.650 --> 19:14.319
I sure hope Chishiya and Ann are okay.

19:14.820 --> 19:16.613
Those two will be just fine.

19:17.239 --> 19:18.157
They're super smart.

19:18.657 --> 19:19.658
That's for sure.

19:20.159 --> 19:21.118
At any rate,

19:21.660 --> 19:25.080
let's gather what we need
so that we can survive the night.

19:25.873 --> 19:26.707
Okay.

19:27.708 --> 19:30.335
Dang, I could fall asleep here.

19:31.503 --> 19:33.922
But who knows
when the King of Spades will come.

19:35.090 --> 19:36.466
Why don't we find some food?

19:38.051 --> 19:40.137
I'll go get us a car.

19:41.221 --> 19:42.181
You come with me.

19:42.848 --> 19:43.849
What? Why?

19:43.932 --> 19:45.684
I know a good place near here.

19:46.560 --> 19:47.686
Oh, all right.

19:51.398 --> 19:54.193
Okay, you two. Get us some good food.

19:54.693 --> 19:55.861
- Will do.
- Here.

19:56.361 --> 19:57.196
Thanks.

19:57.696 --> 19:59.448
- Okay, let's go.
- What are you doing?

19:59.948 --> 20:02.284
Don't whine. I know you've never had
a hot babe on your arm.

20:02.367 --> 20:03.285
Come on.

20:03.368 --> 20:04.411
So what if I haven't?

20:12.628 --> 20:14.880
This is the place. Cool, isn't it?

20:15.380 --> 20:18.133
You're right.
There are a ton of old cars here.

20:18.217 --> 20:20.552
They're called "classic cars."

20:20.636 --> 20:21.887
Who cares what they're called.

20:27.643 --> 20:29.895
Whoa! Holy shit!

20:30.395 --> 20:32.856
This is freaking awesome!

20:32.940 --> 20:34.524
What a perfect body!

20:35.108 --> 20:37.945
Quit touching it!
Are you some kind of molester?

20:38.028 --> 20:40.739
Damn! These body lines are incredible!

20:40.822 --> 20:41.907
What a creep.

20:46.828 --> 20:51.458
I bet the rich were hurt the most
when they were sent to this world.

20:52.542 --> 20:56.088
They worked so hard to make money,
but now it's all worthless.

20:57.256 --> 20:58.340
Good point.

20:59.174 --> 21:00.550
This was probably good for me.

21:01.051 --> 21:03.220
I got out of paying all my back rent.

21:03.720 --> 21:06.974
Me too.
I was released from credit card hell.

21:13.021 --> 21:13.855
But…

21:17.776 --> 21:20.487
I'd still like to go back
even with all that debt.

21:25.033 --> 21:26.118
That's true.

21:54.271 --> 21:57.190
YAKISOBA KORE! BAN
SHORTCAKE FLAVOR

22:00.277 --> 22:02.279
Shortcake-flavored yakisoba!

22:03.155 --> 22:05.574
I saw the TV ad for this!

22:05.657 --> 22:06.533
Me too!

22:07.909 --> 22:09.161
Are you guys nuts?

22:09.244 --> 22:11.121
Have those weird flavors
ever been any good?

22:11.997 --> 22:13.707
This one might be.

22:16.084 --> 22:17.127
No wonder you're a virgin.

22:17.711 --> 22:19.254
What's that got to do with this?

22:20.339 --> 22:22.132
- You'd better eat the whole thing!
- I will!

22:22.215 --> 22:23.717
- Swear it!
- Don't worry. I will.

22:23.800 --> 22:25.177
- You promised.
- Arisu will too.

22:25.260 --> 22:26.261
I'll give it a try.

22:37.481 --> 22:38.940
I wonder if I can finish one.

23:00.212 --> 23:01.046
Welcome!

23:05.842 --> 23:08.386
I like hearing that. It's been a while.

23:09.846 --> 23:10.722
Here.

23:15.727 --> 23:16.895
Is this any good?

23:17.395 --> 23:19.064
Yeah… I'm pretty sure.

23:23.902 --> 23:25.320
How many chopsticks would you like?

23:26.279 --> 23:28.156
Four, please.

23:28.240 --> 23:29.407
Certainly.

23:32.828 --> 23:35.080
Thank you. Please come again.

23:35.872 --> 23:38.708
You know,
your voice sounds an octave higher.

23:39.376 --> 23:40.710
Makes you eager to return, right?

23:43.171 --> 23:45.132
I bet a lot of guys would come to see you.

23:46.091 --> 23:46.967
Because you're pretty.

23:47.551 --> 23:48.385
What?

23:48.468 --> 23:49.469
What?

23:52.722 --> 23:53.890
Did you blush?

23:54.391 --> 23:55.308
No.

23:55.809 --> 23:57.018
I'm used to hearing that.

23:57.727 --> 23:58.562
Really?

24:06.778 --> 24:09.030
I wish I could have worked
at a convenience store.

24:09.573 --> 24:11.032
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

24:11.783 --> 24:14.077
I want to scan the barcodes.

24:15.412 --> 24:18.582
You know those expert cashiers
who are very quick?

24:19.416 --> 24:20.417
I admire them.

24:22.752 --> 24:25.046
I'd like to go back.

24:28.258 --> 24:32.554
I'd eat a steaming hot bowl of yakisoba
in a shop with the AC blasting

24:33.263 --> 24:35.348
while reading the latest manga.

24:47.444 --> 24:48.528
Cut that out.

24:49.529 --> 24:51.740
Quit leering at that. You look creepy.

24:52.324 --> 24:53.366
I can't help it.

24:54.492 --> 24:56.661
- Just look at this, would you?
- What?

24:56.745 --> 24:59.831
Look at her expression… and her boobs!

25:00.332 --> 25:01.458
They're awesome!

25:01.541 --> 25:03.210
That's a manga magazine.

25:03.293 --> 25:05.378
The mangas are the main part,
not the pin-up girls.

25:05.462 --> 25:07.964
- No, they aren't!
- Hey, hey. Let me see!

25:09.925 --> 25:12.260
- See? Nice, aren't they?
- You choking on your food?

25:12.344 --> 25:14.471
- Quit sounding like that.
- Karube. Look.

25:14.554 --> 25:16.723
- Just look. Here. See?
- Arisu.

25:17.474 --> 25:20.268
Keep doing that stuff,
and his virginity will rub off on you.

25:20.977 --> 25:22.979
- Hey! Cut that out!
- Don't give it to me!

25:23.063 --> 25:25.232
- You can't get it from me!
- Oh no! You've got it now!

25:25.315 --> 25:27.275
Wait! I'm already a virgin!

25:34.741 --> 25:36.785
Those were the best of times.

25:43.458 --> 25:44.334
Usagi…

25:47.963 --> 25:49.631
Let's go back for sure.

25:59.057 --> 25:59.891
What's wrong?

26:12.862 --> 26:14.990
KENICHIRO SHIBASAKI ATTEMPTS SUICIDE
OVER FALSE ARTICLE

26:15.073 --> 26:16.533
OKITA ARRESTED FOR COCAINE POSSESSION

26:18.618 --> 26:19.536
Father?

26:25.542 --> 26:27.669
- Mr. Usagi?
- You're Shigenori Usagi, right?

26:29.504 --> 26:32.090
A famous Japanese male mountaineer
has gone missing

26:32.173 --> 26:38.346
while climbing Mt. Tanigawa on the border
of Gunma and Niigata Prefectures.

26:38.430 --> 26:43.601
According to authorities,
the missing man is Shigenori Usagi,

26:43.685 --> 26:47.564
who has climbed Mt. Everest
and works as a mountaineering guide.

26:47.647 --> 26:49.524
…but they still have
yet to find any leads.

26:49.607 --> 26:52.694
Shigenori Usagi appears to have
had a mishap while climbing Mt. Tanigawa,

26:52.777 --> 26:57.115
and though the search for him continues,
no useful leads…

26:57.198 --> 26:58.116
Usagi?

27:03.455 --> 27:04.372
What's wrong?

27:09.502 --> 27:10.503
Arisu…

27:13.089 --> 27:15.467
Was your life before that much fun?

27:17.218 --> 27:18.053
What?

27:22.932 --> 27:24.225
Before coming here,

27:28.730 --> 27:30.148
my father died.

27:36.196 --> 27:37.364
My father…

27:41.159 --> 27:43.411
was called a liar by everyone.

27:45.580 --> 27:46.790
He'd been driven to the edge.

27:52.128 --> 27:53.213
He went to the mountains

27:55.131 --> 27:56.549
and never came back.

28:03.765 --> 28:05.433
He was a mountaineer,

28:10.230 --> 28:12.357
but it wasn't a very high mountain…

28:14.401 --> 28:16.945
so I never thought he could die there.

28:19.322 --> 28:20.281
But…

28:22.075 --> 28:23.993
I've learned something
living in this world.

28:28.581 --> 28:29.582
I think my father…

28:33.503 --> 28:34.546
also wanted…

28:38.133 --> 28:40.218
to live in a different world.

28:44.556 --> 28:45.932
His way of thinking…

28:52.021 --> 28:52.897
Now…

28:55.191 --> 28:56.651
I can understand it well.

29:00.655 --> 29:01.656
Even now…

29:05.452 --> 29:07.203
I'd hate that world if I went back.

29:16.087 --> 29:17.005
I'm sorry.

29:19.758 --> 29:21.760
I know everyone
is trying so hard to go back.

29:32.020 --> 29:32.937
Usagi.

29:34.981 --> 29:36.483
I understand that feeling too.

29:38.485 --> 29:39.402
I really do.

29:43.239 --> 29:46.826
I also thought that
the world was a bunch of crap.

29:48.703 --> 29:49.871
But not anymore.

29:51.539 --> 29:52.415
Now…

29:53.917 --> 29:55.585
I want to go back to that world…

29:57.837 --> 29:59.547
and start over again.

30:06.262 --> 30:09.682
I'll protect you, Usagi,
even if it costs my life.

30:12.018 --> 30:13.269
So let's go back together.

30:26.866 --> 30:27.700
I'm sorry…

30:32.372 --> 30:33.790
Everyone says…

30:35.416 --> 30:37.126
they understand how I feel.

30:38.545 --> 30:40.964
They tell me to
forget the past and cheer up.

30:47.846 --> 30:50.348
But there's no way
people can understand it so easily.

30:52.934 --> 30:54.018
I mean…

30:56.396 --> 30:58.565
I can't see into your heart, Arisu.

31:03.820 --> 31:06.489
I don't want you to
feel like you understand me.

31:09.576 --> 31:10.410
It's just that…

31:14.747 --> 31:17.166
when I'm asked if I want to go back…

31:19.878 --> 31:20.795
I…

31:27.594 --> 31:29.596
I think this place might be better.

31:31.264 --> 31:34.434
But if you stay here, you'll never…

31:47.864 --> 31:48.865
Let's go back.

31:50.909 --> 31:52.076
They'll be waiting.

32:29.781 --> 32:33.034
Arisu! Usagi! Hop in!

32:33.826 --> 32:35.411
We're way too exposed like this.

32:35.495 --> 32:36.996
It's the only one that runs.

32:37.080 --> 32:39.499
Liar! You just fell in love with it.

32:39.582 --> 32:42.001
You said it had a "sexy body."
God, that's weird!

32:42.085 --> 32:44.170
I said "perfect body"!

32:44.253 --> 32:45.463
What a creep!

32:45.546 --> 32:47.840
"Creep"? How can you call me a creep?

32:51.094 --> 32:51.928
Hop in.

32:59.227 --> 33:00.228
Arisu.

33:00.812 --> 33:01.688
Yeah.

34:06.878 --> 34:08.880
The King of Spades is getting closer.

34:10.214 --> 34:13.217
The whole city is his Game Arena.

34:16.387 --> 34:19.724
Then we'll just have to
keep running from him.

34:22.727 --> 34:24.687
There's one way
to keep from being attacked.

34:26.064 --> 34:26.898
What is it?

34:28.357 --> 34:29.817
Participate in another game.

34:30.985 --> 34:31.819
What?

34:33.905 --> 34:35.615
If I were one of them,

34:36.741 --> 34:39.160
I would never interfere
in the others' games.

34:39.911 --> 34:42.288
The bare minimum of manners among enemies.

34:43.831 --> 34:46.125
They never interfere in other games.

34:47.543 --> 34:51.380
All the games have
strict rules that they follow.

34:52.256 --> 34:56.677
If games intruded on each other,
they would break down.

34:57.678 --> 34:58.513
But…

34:59.639 --> 35:01.432
I don't want to join any games.

35:02.600 --> 35:05.645
Either way, the King of Spades
has forced us to join this one.

35:06.896 --> 35:08.314
If we keep hiding like this,

35:08.940 --> 35:11.609
either we'll eventually get found
and killed by the King of Spades

35:11.692 --> 35:13.402
or our visas will run out.

35:14.570 --> 35:17.990
Since they're the people
who make the games,

35:19.117 --> 35:21.702
we might be able to find out
what this world is

35:22.620 --> 35:24.038
or why we have to play these games.

35:26.165 --> 35:27.500
I want to know why…

35:29.752 --> 35:31.420
all these people have had to die.

35:43.391 --> 35:44.767
Let's vote on it.

35:47.145 --> 35:48.437
I'm with Arisu.

35:54.193 --> 35:56.112
Okay. I am too.

35:58.072 --> 35:59.115
What about you, Usagi?

36:03.119 --> 36:04.370
Majority rules, right?

36:05.037 --> 36:06.581
You've already got your answer.

36:09.625 --> 36:11.878
If that's the case, where will we go?

36:16.841 --> 36:20.469
Of all the cards I can see,
this one's the farthest away.

36:21.512 --> 36:22.722
How about the King of Clubs?

36:23.431 --> 36:25.766
Hold on! We're starting with a king?

36:26.434 --> 36:29.103
A king probably has better information.

36:29.729 --> 36:31.189
You've sure got guts.

36:32.064 --> 36:35.568
What's more, club games require teamwork.

36:36.611 --> 36:38.279
So we've got a chance of winning.

36:39.697 --> 36:40.907
With us on the same team.

36:41.407 --> 36:42.241
That's for sure!

36:42.742 --> 36:43.993
I'm not so sure about you.

36:44.076 --> 36:44.911
Hey!

38:01.153 --> 38:02.071
Look.

38:03.030 --> 38:05.157
NO WEAPONS ALLOWED

38:16.043 --> 38:18.296
NO WEAPONS ALLOWED

38:18.796 --> 38:22.925
PARTICIPANTS: 5
PUT ON A BRACELET AND WAIT

38:23.009 --> 38:25.636
It says there are five participants.

38:26.804 --> 38:27.805
But there are only four.

38:29.598 --> 38:31.809
At last, we've got five people.

38:37.148 --> 38:38.232
Niragi…

38:38.316 --> 38:39.692
It's been a while.

38:43.404 --> 38:46.365
You mean… you're alive?

38:49.535 --> 38:51.329
I can't be on a team with that jerk!

38:52.330 --> 38:53.748
We'll never clear this game.

38:55.624 --> 38:57.835
He'll never cooperate with us.

38:57.918 --> 38:59.837
This isn't coming off.

39:02.715 --> 39:05.301
And my only goal is to enjoy these games.

39:06.969 --> 39:09.180
If you don't want
to play this game with me,

39:09.263 --> 39:11.182
then you can just fuck off.

39:16.479 --> 39:17.438
Usagi?

39:18.606 --> 39:20.483
Who cares what his goal is?

39:27.990 --> 39:31.619
If we don't take part in a game,
we'll eventually die anyway.

39:33.579 --> 39:34.580
In that case…

39:37.208 --> 39:39.418
I've already made up my mind
to fight and survive.

39:44.840 --> 39:45.841
Me too.

39:50.262 --> 39:51.430
I want some answers.

40:09.073 --> 40:10.324
You idiots.

40:11.784 --> 40:13.285
Don't blame me for what will happen.

40:18.916 --> 40:20.251
Don't hold us back.

40:21.293 --> 40:23.379
Teamwork is key in this game.

40:25.548 --> 40:28.509
I wouldn't be so sure
who will be holding who back.

40:36.392 --> 40:38.394
Registration is complete.

40:38.894 --> 40:41.313
Proceed to the Game Arena.

41:47.087 --> 41:48.339
What is this place?

41:54.553 --> 41:56.972
The King of Clubs team has arrived.

42:19.370 --> 42:20.371
Welcome…

42:22.498 --> 42:24.124
to our Game Arena.

42:26.293 --> 42:27.836
I'm the King of Clubs…

42:29.421 --> 42:30.256
Kyuma.

42:45.187 --> 42:46.230
Okay.

42:46.313 --> 42:49.984
I'll introduce the other members.
Starting over there, that's Shitara.

42:54.196 --> 42:55.030
Uta.

42:56.240 --> 42:57.241
Maki.

42:58.993 --> 43:00.035
Goken.

43:03.497 --> 43:04.498
Nice to meet you.

43:08.419 --> 43:10.170
Why are you guys so quiet?

43:10.796 --> 43:12.464
You're freaking them out.

43:12.548 --> 43:13.924
Put on some pants, would you?

43:14.008 --> 43:16.218
What? Why?

43:16.719 --> 43:18.887
Nudists have been around for centuries.

43:18.971 --> 43:20.973
It's a perfectly legit lifestyle.

43:22.850 --> 43:24.935
Wearing clothes is a social construct.

43:25.519 --> 43:27.771
But there's no biological need for them.

43:28.647 --> 43:32.985
Living life in our natural state
is humanity's true form.

43:34.445 --> 43:35.988
What is this dude's problem?

43:37.865 --> 43:39.533
This is the King of Clubs?

43:40.534 --> 43:41.869
He's lost his marbles.

43:43.412 --> 43:44.663
Never mind that.

43:45.372 --> 43:46.790
Who the heck are you people?

43:50.294 --> 43:51.378
Who are we?

43:52.546 --> 43:54.715
We're the citizens of this country.

43:57.551 --> 43:58.427
The "citizens"?

43:59.178 --> 44:01.013
That's right. The citizens.

46:48.931 --> 46:53.936
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
